DEBUG_SAULO, temporary: a fixed ring of 65536 compact audio events (packets and frames the XMA contexts decode, FFmpeg
errors by kind, buffer advances and swaps, waits for the other input buffer, guest input buffer changes, loop jumps,
decoder reopens, stalls, full or starved output, context allocate/clear/release, slow XMADisableContext, late guest
submits, late or empty output callbacks and the output queue depth every 100 ms). Writers take a slot with one
fetch_add and publish it with a sequence number, without locks. history::Dump() starts a thread that logs the last
5 seconds between "DEBUG_SAULO AUDIO SNAPSHOT BEGIN" and "... END", waits 2 seconds and logs what followed between
"DEBUG_SAULO AUDIO SNAPSHOT POST" and "... POST END". The port calls it on F9.

